{
  "capitulo": 7,
  "titulo_es": "Quiero que vengas",
  "titulo": { "en": "I want you to come" },
  "intro": { "en": "When you want someone else to do something, Spanish uses the subjunctive." },
  "palabras": {
    "quiero que": { "en": "I want (someone) to", "pron": "KYE-ro ke", "cat": "expression" },
    "vengas": { "en": "you come (subjunctive)", "pron": "BEN-gas", "cat": "verb" },
    "hables": { "en": "you speak (subjunctive)", "pron": "A-bles", "cat": "verb" },
    "estés": { "en": "you are (subjunctive of estar)", "pron": "es-TES", "cat": "verb" },
    "espero que": { "en": "I hope that", "pron": "es-PE-ro ke", "cat": "expression" },
    "la fiesta": { "en": "the party", "pron": "la FYES-ta", "genero": "f" },
    "más despacio": { "en": "more slowly", "pron": "mas des-PA-thyo", "cat": "expression" }
  },
  "bloques": [
    {
      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": "Same person, or another person",
      "texto": "If the subject stays the same, use the infinitive: **quiero venir**.\n\nIf you want **another person** to act, use **que** + present subjunctive: **quiero que vengas**.\n\nThe present subjunctive of regular verbs swaps the vowel: habla → **hable**, come → **coma**, vive → **viva**.\n\n**Espero que estés** bien. Hope about someone else works the same way."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tabla",
      "titulo": "Hablar, present subjunctive",
      "columnas": ["Person", "hablar"],
      "filas": [
        ["yo", "hable"],
        ["tú", "hables"],
        ["él / ella / usted", "hable"],
        ["nosotros", "hablemos"],
        ["vosotros", "habléis"],
        ["ellos / ustedes", "hablen"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "dialogo",
      "titulo": "The party",
      "frases": [
        {
          "quien": "Lucía",
          "es": "Quiero que vengas a la fiesta.",
          "en": "I want you to come to the party.",
          "analisis": [
            ["Quiero", "I want"],
            ["que vengas", "that you come"],
            ["a la fiesta", "to the party"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Pablo",
          "es": "Quiero venir, pero trabajo.",
          "en": "I want to come, but I'm working.",
          "nota": "Same subject, so the infinitive: quiero venir.",
          "analisis": [
            ["Quiero venir", "I want to come"],
            ["pero trabajo", "but I work"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Lucía",
          "es": "Espero que estés bien.",
          "en": "I hope you're well.",
          "analisis": [
            ["Espero que", "I hope that"],
            ["estés bien", "you are well"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Pablo",
          "es": "Habla más despacio. Quiero que hables despacio.",
          "en": "Speak more slowly. I want you to speak slowly.",
          "analisis": [
            ["Habla", "command"],
            ["Quiero que hables", "I want you to speak"]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "vocabulario",
      "palabras": ["quiero que", "vengas", "hables", "estés", "espero que", "la fiesta", "más despacio"]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "test",
      "id": "b1-subj-mismo",
      "pregunta": { "en": "You want to come yourself. Which sentence?" },
      "opciones": {
        "Quiero venir": { "en": "Same person: infinitive." },
        "Quiero que venga": { "en": "That asks someone else to come." },
        "Quiero que vengas": { "en": "That asks tú to come." }
      },
      "correcta": "Quiero venir"
    },
    {
      "tipo": "huecos",
      "id": "b1-subj-vengas",
      "pregunta": { "en": "Complete: I want you to come." },
      "frase": "Quiero que ___ a la fiesta.",
      "audio": true,
      "opciones": {
        "vengas": { "en": "Another person after quiero que: subjunctive." },
        "vienes": { "en": "Vienes is the ordinary present." },
        "venir": { "en": "The infinitive is only when the subject does not change." }
      },
      "correcta": "vengas"
    }
  ]
}
